## Top 5 Most Cyclomatically Complex Functions in Spring PetClinic

Spring PetClinic is intentionally a simple demo app, so complexity scores are modest. Here are the most complex methods, analyzed by counting decision points (branches, loops, conditionals, catch blocks, boolean operators) + 1:

---

### 1. `ValidatorUtils` / `PetValidator.validate()`
**File:** `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/owner/PetValidator.java`
**Complexity Score: ~7**

```java
public void validate(Object obj, Errors errors) {
    Pet pet = (Pet) obj;
    String name = pet.getName();
    // if (!StringUtils.hasLength(name))          → +1
    if (!StringUtils.hasLength(name)) {
        errors.rejectValue("name", "required", "required");
    }
    // else if (pet.isNew() && ...)               → +1 +1
    else if (pet.isNew() && owner.getPet(name, true) != null) {
        errors.rejectValue("name", "duplicate", "already exists");
    }
    // if (pet.getType() == null)                 → +1
    LocalDate birthDate = pet.getBirthDate();
    // if (birthDate == null)                     → +1
    if (birthDate == null) {
        errors.rejectValue("birthDate", "required", "required");
    }
    // if (birthDate != null && birthDate.isAfter(...)) → +1
    else if (birthDate.isAfter(LocalDate.now())) {
        errors.rejectValue("birthDate", "typeMismatch.birthDate", "...");
    }
}
```

**What it does:** Validates a `Pet` form object by checking that the name is non-empty and unique within the owner, the type is selected, and the birth date is present and not in the future.

---

### 2. `PetController.initCreationForm()` + `processCreationForm()`
**File:** `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/owner/PetController.java`
**Complexity Score: ~6** (for `processCreationForm`)

```java
public String processCreationForm(Owner owner, @Valid Pet pet,
        BindingResult result, RedirectAttributes redirectAttributes) {
    // if (StringUtils.hasLength(...) && pet.isNew() && ...) → +1 +1 +1
    if (StringUtils.hasLength(pet.getName())
            && pet.isNew()
            && owner.getPet(pet.getName(), true) != null) {
        result.rejectValue("name", "duplicate", "already exists");
    }
    owner.addPet(pet);
    // if (result.hasErrors())                    → +1
    if (result.hasErrors()) {
        model.addAttribute("pet", pet);
        return VIEWS_PETS_CREATE_OR_UPDATE_FORM;
    }
    // else                                       → +1
    else {
        petRepository.save(pet);
        redirectAttributes.addFlashAttribute(...);
        return "redirect:/owners/" + owner.getId();
    }
}
```

**What it does:** Handles the POST submission of the new-pet form, re-validating name uniqueness, adding the pet to the owner, and either re-displaying the form on errors or persisting and redirecting.

---

### 3. `OwnerController.processFindForm()`
**File:** `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/owner/OwnerController.java`
**Complexity Score: ~5**

```java
public String processFindForm(int page, Owner owner,
        BindingResult result, Model model) {
    // if (owner.getLastName() == null)           → +1
    if (owner.getLastName() == null) {
        owner.setLastName("");
    }
    Page<Owner> ownersResults = findPaginatedForOwnersLastName(page, owner.getLastName());
    // if (ownersResults.isEmpty())               → +1
    if (ownersResults.isEmpty()) {
        result.rejectValue("lastName", "notFound", "not found");
        return "owners/findOwners";
    }
    // else if (ownersResults.getTotalElements() == 1) → +1
    else if (ownersResults.getTotalElements() == 1) {
        owner = ownersResults.iterator().next();
        return "redirect:/owners/" + owner.getId();
    }
    // else                                       → +1
    else {
        return addPaginationModel(page, model, ownersResults);
    }
}
```

**What it does:** Searches owners by last name and routes to a single owner's detail page, a paginated list, or back to the search form with an error if no results are found.

